"Control systems on Lie groups. (https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720060315)\nciteturn0search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 54.2 years ago; Crawled: last month; Control systems on Lie groups.The controllability properties of systems which are described by an evolution equation in a Lie group are studied. ... Jurdjevic, V. ... Sussmann, H.\n\nControl systems on Lie groups.The controllability properties of systems which are described by an evolution equation in a Lie group are studied. The revelant Lie algebras induced by a right invariant system are singled out, and the basic properties of attainable sets are derived. The homogeneous case and the general case are studied, and results are interpreted in terms of controllability. Five examples are given.\n\nDocument ID\n\n19720060315\n\nAcquisition Source\n\nLegacy CDMS\n\nDocument Type\n\nReprint (Version printed in journal)\n\nExternal Source(s)\n\ndoi:10.1016/0022-0396(72)90035-6\n\nAuthors\n\nJurdjevic, V. (Toronto, University Toronto, Canada)\n\nSussmann, H. J. (Chicago, University Chicago, Ill., United States)\n\nDate Acquired\n\nAugust 6, 2013\n\nPublication Date\n\nSeptember 1, 1972\n\nPublication Information\n\nPublication: Journal of Differential Equations\n\nVolume: 12\n\nSubject Category\n\nMathematics\n\nAccession Number\n\n72A43981\n\nFunding Number(s)\n\nCONTRACT_GRANT: N00014-67-0298-0006\n\nCONTRACT_GRANT: NGR-22-007-172\n\nDistribution Limits\n\nPublic\n\n### Available Downloads\n\nThere are no available downloads for this record.\n\nvisibility_off No Preview Available--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIndependent random utility representations (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0165489602000203)\nciteturn0search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; A procedure, called mixture technique, is developed which allows one to construct a new point in I_{LO}^{n} and its independent representation from known points in I_{LO}^{n}. ... An overview of the connection of P_{LO}^{n} to random utility theory is given by Fishburn (1992), Suck (1992) and Koppen (1995).\n\n## Mathematical Social Sciences\n\nDate: July 2002\n\nPages: 371-389\n\nVolume: Volume 43, Issue 3\n\n## Part of special issue\n\n# Independent random utility representations\n\nAuthor links open overlay panel Reinhard Suck\n\nShow more\n\nCite\n\nAdd to Mendeley\n\nShare\n\n10.1016/S0165-4896(02)00020-3\n\nAccess through your organizationPurchase PDF\n\n\n## Abstract\n\nThe question of the existence of independent random variables which represent a given set of binary choice data is investigated. It is related to the linear ordering polytope. The subset of it which is independently representable, denoted by I_{LO}^{n}, is characterized for three elements. For the general case, necessary conditions are given and their geometric meaning is discussed. A procedure, called mixture technique, is developed which allows one to construct a new point in I_{LO}^{n} and its independent representation from known points in I_{LO}^{n}. Finally, a few results on parametric representations are derived.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nControl systems on Lie groups (https://explore.openaire.eu/search/publication?pid=10.1016%2F0022-0396%2872%2990035-6)\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 54.2 years ago; Crawled: last month; Control systems on Lie groups ... Authors: Jurdjevic, Velimir; Sussmann, Héctor J; ... The controllability properties of systems which are described by an evolution equation in a Lie group are studied.\n\n# \n\nControl systems on Lie groups\n\ndescription Publication keyboard_double_arrow_right Article 01 Sep 1972 English Publisher:Elsevier BV Journal:Journal of Differential Equations, volume 12, pages 313-329 (issn: 0022-0396, Copyright policy )\n\nAuthors: Jurdjevic, Velimir; Sussmann, Héctor J;\n\ndoi: 10.1016/0022-0396(72)90035-6\n\n# \n\nControl systems on Lie groups\n\n  *     * Summary\n\n  *     * Subjects\n\n  *     * Metrics\n\nAbstract\n\nThe controllability properties of systems which are described by an evolution equation in a Lie group are studied. The revelant Lie algebras induced by a right invariant system are singled out, and the basic properties of attainable sets are derived. The homogeneous case and the general case are studied, and results are interpreted in terms of controllability. Five examples are given.\n\nRelated Organizations\n\n  * University of Toronto\n\nCanada\n\n  * University of Chicago\n\nUnited States\n\n  * Department of Mathematics\n  * THE UNIVERSITY OF CHICAGO\n\nUnited States\n\nKeywords\n\nControl/observation systems governed by functional relations other than differential equations (such as hybrid and switching systems), Control/observation systems in abstract spaces, Analysis--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nControl systems on Lie groups (https://www.researchwithrutgers.org/en/publications/control-systems-on-lie-groups/)\nciteturn0search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 54.2 years ago; Crawled: last month; Jurdjevic, V & Sussmann, HJ 1972, 'Control systems on Lie groups', Journal of Differential Equations, vol. 12, no. 2, pp.\n\n# Control systems on Lie groups\n\n  * Velimir Jurdjevic\n  * , Héctor J. Sussmann\n\n  * School of Arts and Sciences, Mathematics\n\nResearch output: Contribution to journal › Article › peer-review\n\n472   Link opens in a new tab Scopus citations\n\nOriginal language  | English (US)\nPages (from-to)  | 313-329\nNumber of pages  | 17\nJournal  | Journal of Differential Equations\nVolume  | 12\nIssue number  | 2\nDOIs  | \n\n  * https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-0396(72)90035-6\nState  | Published - Sep 1972\n\n## All Science Journal Classification (ASJC) codes\n\n  * Analysis\n  * Applied Mathematics\n\n## Access to Document\n\n  * 10.1016/0022-0396(72)90035-6\n\n## Cite this\n\n  * APA\n  * Author\n  * BIBTEX\n  * Harvard\n  * 